<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kurt Hahn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1886–1974</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kurt Hahn was a German-born educator. Secretary and adviser to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-maximilian-of-baden">Prince Maximilian of Baden</a>, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schule-schloss-salem">Schule Schloss Salem</a> boarding school with him in 1920. Arrested after criticising the Nazis, he left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1933, where he founded Gordonstoun school in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. He also founded the Outward Bound movement and the United World Colleges and inspired the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>'s Award.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kurt-hahn.jpg" alt="Kurt Hahn" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ryswyles · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurt_Hahn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
